{
  "about": "A typical spine for what one front film cannot show: forward lean, front-to-back wedge and depth of each vertebral body, and twist. Typical values with their spread between people, not measurements of any patient. Side profiles are one adult's bone posture scaled to cohort kyphosis (T5 upper to T12 lower endplate) and lordosis (L1 upper to L5 lower endplate) for each curve size, and levelled so the line from T1's centre to L5's centre is upright. Angles in degrees, lengths in millimetres, levels C7 to L5. Built by bone-prep/typical_spine.py; bone-prep/typical-spine.md gives every source and step.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "key": "bodyparts3d",
      "citation": "BodyParts3D 4.0, The Database Center for Life Science, licensed under CC Attribution 4.0 International. One adult man's anatomy from whole-body MRI.",
      "gives": "The per-level shape of the side profile, body widths, depth-to-width proportions, each body's own side wedge and the stacking spread."
    },
    {
      "key": "burkus2018",
      "citation": "Burkus M, Schlégl ÁT, O'Sullivan I, Márkus I, Vermes C, Tunyogi-Csapó M. Sagittal plane assessment of spino-pelvic complex in a Central European population with adolescent idiopathic scoliosis: a case control study. Scoliosis Spinal Disord 2018;13:10. DOI 10.1186/s13013-018-0156-0. Full text read.",
      "gives": "Kyphosis T5-T12 of 69 young people without scoliosis, 32.9 (SD 15.0) degrees; lordosis L1-L5, 46.0 (9.1) without and 46.4 (13.2) with scoliosis, not different."
    },
    {
      "key": "sullivan2020",
      "citation": "Sullivan TB, Bastrom TP, Bartley CE, Dolan LA, Weinstein SL, Newton PO. More severe thoracic idiopathic scoliosis is associated with a greater three-dimensional loss of thoracic kyphosis. Spine Deform 2020;8(6):1205-1211. DOI 10.1007/s43390-020-00149-7. Abstract only.",
      "gives": "Three-dimensional kyphosis T5-T12 of 3032 patients: 13 (SD 10) degrees for curves of 20 to 45 degrees, 5 (12) for curves over 45."
    },
    {
      "key": "newton2015",
      "citation": "Newton PO, Fujimori T, Doan J, Reighard FG, Bastrom TP, Misaghi A. Defining the \"three-dimensional sagittal plane\" in thoracic adolescent idiopathic scoliosis. J Bone Joint Surg Am 2015;97(20):1694-1701. DOI 10.2106/JBJS.O.00148. Abstract only.",
      "gives": "A mean curve of 55 degrees for a group whose three-dimensional kyphosis T5-T12 was 6 (SD 14) degrees, used to place the curves over 45 degrees."
    },
    {
      "key": "macthiong2007",
      "citation": "Mac-Thiong JM, Labelle H, Berthonnaud E, Betz RR, Roussouly P. Sagittal spinopelvic balance in normal children and adolescents. Eur Spine J 2007;16(2):227-234. DOI 10.1007/s00586-005-0013-8. Abstract only.",
      "gives": "Spread between children of the lean of the thoracic and of the lumbar spine, 5.2 degrees each."
    },
    {
      "key": "jozsef2022",
      "citation": "József K, Schlégl ÁT, Burkus M, Márkus I, O'Sullivan I, Than P, Tunyogi-Csapó M. Maximal axial vertebral rotation in adolescent idiopathic scoliosis: is the apical vertebra the most rotated? Global Spine J 2022;12(2):244-248. DOI 10.1177/2192568220948830. Full text read.",
      "gives": "Apical twist, mean and SD, in six bands of curve size, 332 patients."
    },
    {
      "key": "pan2021",
      "citation": "Pan CL, Zhang BY, Zhu YH, Ma YH, Li MF, Wang X, Yang F, Li YQ, Zhu YH. Morphologic analysis of Chinese lumbar endplate by three-dimensional computed tomography reconstructions for helping design lumbar disc prosthesis. Medicine (Baltimore) 2021;100(6):e24583. DOI 10.1097/MD.0000000000024583. Full text read.",
      "gives": "Spread between people of endplate depth over width, T12 to L5, 150 adults."
    },
    {
      "key": "busscher2010",
      "citation": "Busscher I, Ploegmakers JJ, Verkerke GJ, Veldhuizen AG. Comparative anatomical dimensions of the complete human and porcine spine. Eur Spine J 2010;19(7):1104-1114. DOI 10.1007/s00586-010-1326-9. Full text read.",
      "gives": "Spread of the front and back heights of each vertebral body, C7 to L5, six adult spines."
    }
  ],
